CM_ BO_ 184 "Motorsteuergerät";
CM_ BO_ 192 "Motorsteuergerät";
CM_ BO_ 219 "AEB_Object_Status and AEB_Object_Status_B values 4 and 5/6 coincide with AEB potentially activating";
CM_ SG_ 219 AEB_Target_Decel "Scale is estimated. Lowest request seen was -6.99";
CM_ SG_ 219 AEB_TTC_Countdown "Can count down to zero before AEB activates, but may not always precede an AEB or mean it will happen";
CM_ SG_ 219 VRU_Detected "Commonly high when a pedestrian is seen. Also goes high with AWV_Unavailable";
CM_ SG_ 219 AWV_Unavailable "High when the AWV function cannot operate, seen with the radar obstructed and with the powertrain ECU off the bus. MEB_AWV_01.AWV_Status carries the same state";
CM_ SG_ 219 AWV_Init_Status "Power-up state only, reads 2 once running. Does not report whether AEB can operate, use AWV_Unavailable for that";
CM_ SG_ 219 Unknown_192 "Constant per platform (0 on all gen1 ID.4/Born, 1 on all gen2 ID.4)";
CM_ SG_ 219 Unknown_27 "Low bit tracks AWV_Unavailable, but is also set in 20-33% of normal driving";
CM_ SG_ 219 Unknown_80 "Low bit is normally 1 and clears with AWV_Unavailable, but also clears in ~1% of normal driving";
CM_ SG_ 313 Long_Control_Inhibit "Goes high after user brakes hard, causes temporary TSK_Status fault";
CM_ SG_ 333 SET_ME_0x2FE "Only set by stock ACC on 2024+; reads 0 on pre-2024 and is not packed by mebcan";
CM_ SG_ 380196013 AWV_Status "Mirrors AWV_03.AWV_Unavailable, at a higher rate";
